OL,3,GNEWSAFarmer urges shops to buy British
OL,4,Astrawberries
OL,5,
OL,6,FA fruit farmer has urged supermarkets
OL,7,Fto keep buying British produce over the
OL,8,Fautumn after summer heatwaves led to
OL,9,Fbumper crops of strawberries.
OL,11,FRobert Rendall, the managing director
OL,12,Fof Boxford Farms in Suffolk, said
OL,13,Fsupermarkets begin to import more
OL,14,Fproduce from abroad during autumn, but
OL,15,FBritish strawberries - which usually
OL,16,Freach peak sweetness in June and July -
OL,17,Fwere still healthy.
OL,19,F"The message we're trying to get out
OL,20,Fthere is there's still good quality UK
OL,21,Ffruit in volume, and we'd love to see
OL,22,Fthose sold right through to the autumn.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,380,370,200,160,0,100
